    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2TbsaN4fF9KT3pfs4GMnNSt)_\n\n## Summary\nHovering a `[cite:@key]` link raised `void-function citar-get-template` (muted by safe_call), so neither the tooltip nor the echo area showed anything. `citar-get-template` and `citar-format--entry` (as called) are not part of citar's current API.\n\n- `sp-cite-hover--reference` now uses the public `citar-format-reference`, which applies the `preview` template of `citar-templates`.\n- Errors from citar give nil (tooltip then shows \"not found in the bibliography\"), so a hover never signals.\n- Doc (`sp-academic.org`, \"Citation hover\") edited and tangled to `sp-citations.el`; CHANGELOG entry added.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] New `tests/sp-cite-hover-test.el` (Emacs 29.3, citar stubbed without `citar-get-template`): 4 pass; 3 of them fail on the old code.\n- [x] `tools/check-tangle.sh`: `sp-citations.el` matches its doc.\n- [ ] Not run: the real config. Hover a citekey, and put point on one, to see the tooltip and the echo area text.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9394TzJXj3etWuUEY)_",
